!
! TCPIP$SERVICE.DAT - TCP/IP Services for OVMX auxiliary-server (TCPIP$INETD)
! service database (rd vms-cdb9).
!
! OVMX-DEFINED FORMAT (CLAUDE.md Rule 8): only the auxiliary-server BEHAVIOUR
! (a master listener that binds each enabled service's well-known port and
! spawns the service's image on an inbound connection) is observed from the
! public VSI OpenVMS TCP/IP Services documentation. VSI does NOT publish the
! byte-level layout of its internal service store, so THIS LINE FORMAT is an
! OVMX invention -- the same whitespace-separated text idiom as
! SYS$STARTUP:VMS$VMS.DAT -- parsed by tcpip_inetd_parse_db()
! (src/vmstcpip/services/tcpip_inetd.h). It is NOT presented as VMS-authentic.
!
! One ENABLED service per line:
!
!     service-name  port  image-filespec  [image-args...]
!
! separated by whitespace. "port" is the decimal TCP port the auxiliary server
! binds over the executive BGn: seam; "image-filespec" is the service image the
! auxiliary server runs on an inbound connection (with the accepted connection
! as its SYS$INPUT/SYS$OUTPUT); any trailing tokens are passed to the image as
! arguments. Lines beginning with "!" and blank lines are comments/ignored.
!
! To enable a service, add its line here; the auxiliary server binds it when
! @SYS$STARTUP:TCPIP$STARTUP starts TCPIP$INETD.EXE.
!
! SSH is delivered by VMSSSHD.EXE, launched by the auxiliary server (rd vms-9ef).
! It is listed here but commented out until VMSSSHD.EXE ships in the bootable
! image; uncomment to enable once present (do NOT fake an unbound service).
!
! SSH   22  SYS$SYSTEM:VMSSSHD.EXE
